    <cac:TenderingProcess xmlns="">
        <cbc:ProcedureCode listName="procurement-procedure-type">neg-wo-call</cbc:ProcedureCode>
        <cac:ProcessJustification>
            <cbc:ProcessReasonCode listName="direct-award-justification">technical</cbc:ProcessReasonCode>
            <cbc:ProcessReason languageID="ENG">The current GE Healthcare CT Scanner installed at the Medical Imaging Department at Mater Dei Hospital, is now 9 years ago, but is still a perfectly good working CT Scanner machine, and may still give another 10 years of excellent clinical service to the Medical imaging Department at Mater Dei Hospital. The only issue is that as this machine is a 2015 model, it lacks certain technological capabilities that have become synonymous to today’s world. The main things that are currently missing in this machine are the Artificial Intelligence (AI) capabilities that today has become so synonymous to the medical field in nearly all fronts. As a result of this, and as AI has now become so important to assist clinicians in the diagnoses of various conditions that develop within the human body, that the time has arrived where this CT Scanner Machine requires an overall upgrade that will bring this machine to today’s technological advancements and capabilities, that will greatly facilitate the work of our clinicians that depend so much on this machine. </cbc:ProcessReason>
        </cac:ProcessJustification>
    </cac:TenderingProcess>
